{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/462922-conspiracy-the-cleaners","id":462922,"title":"Conspiracy: the Cleaners","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T18:05:00-07:00","id":462922,"title":"Conspiracy: the Cleaners","content":"(Playing Viscera Cleanup gave me an... irresistible idea.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> &quot;We clean everything, including the system if we need to. Mistakes cannot be tolerated in our line of work.&quot; <br /> <br /> A truck in grey and white stops near the mayor's house. Over the following years, a mother and daughter will wake up crying over something missing, but they don't what, or who, it is. But, why is it the town has no memory of who was mayor all those years ago? <br /> <br /> A school in Washington hires new janitors, and over the course of a week, various faculty will disappear. None of the students care, those missing were loathed after all, and besides, their replacements are much better. But, why do so many complain about the stench of chemicals afterwards? <br /> <br /> Last week, another tragic school massacre occurred, taking the lives of six students, a teacher, and injuring many more. But, why do so many of the victims claim they saw giant wolves? And who commits a massacre with a knife in America? <br /> <br /> A police chief vows to find missing children, but nothing comes of it. Before much can be done, he is killed by his wife who leaves a note taking responsibility. The resulting media storm hides any evidence to the contrary, such as the strange new cleaning staff the city had employed. <br /> <br /> <br /> They are not a government, and while many corporations are subsidiaries of this particular entity, the Cleaners are not a particular private entity. Their real name, if they have one, isn't known, just a whole host of nick names and various fake brand names like the Squeaky Cleaning Company. Their employees did frequently once work as traditional cleaning staff, however enjoy far larger salaries than most in their position would, owing to the extremely difficult nature of their work. Additionally, they have a variety of former news personnel, specifically trained to handle a more social side to cleaning up an incident.<br /> <br /> The Cleaners specialize in removing all evidence of massive supernatural events, whether it is a massacre committed by werewolves, a witch casting a rather large spell, or even something much worse, like some sort of God distorting a local area. Such cleanup is impossible with traditional tools, requiring the mass altering of public and private records, along with human memories. Some incidents are so large that it proves to be easier to instead alter the incident to fit a more mundane version of events. And, in it all, many will be murdered, or worse, just to cover it up. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:52:01-07:00","id":464092,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting premise. I guess the obvious question is... Why? What do these people gain by this? What ideology motivates someone to kill over this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:33:57-07:00","id":467877,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>History</b></div> <br /> The Cleaners are shrouded in mystery, as after all, an organization that has mastered the art of cleaning up mass supernatural acts can rather easily cover their own tracks. Their origins are much the same, with only two things known for sure. The first is that they formed in the 20th Century. The specific country isn't know for sure, however, has been theorized to probably be the United States owing to whom they employ, and their possible relations with American religious cults.<br /> <br /> The second known part about their origins, and the aspect that has shed much light on their motivations, is that they were once a religious cult. From this, some details about their motivations have been gathered, and much has been theorized. The concrete aspect is that the Cleaners seem to be not trying to hide things from humanity so much as hiding specific things from some sort of deity. Why they feel the need to do this seems to be because of the belief that the entire world will end if this deity ever wakes up, which could arise from mass violence.<br /> <br /> Their focus on supernatural events in public spaces, such as schools, and malls, along with an attempt to violently silence witnesses, is evidence of this.<br /> <br /> What adds further proof is that, frequently, the Cleaners have attempted to hide things from supernatural beings. In the 1970s, for example, they not only attempted to hide a massacre committed by a Spirit from humans, but also Werewolves. For the latter, they attempted to wipe out the Spirits in an area, and killed multiple Werewolf packs in a desperate attempt to hide a lot of details about the massacre. Whether they succeeded in hiding specific details from them isn't know, but ironically, it made the Cleaners themselves gain a lot of attention. In the news, the event was hidden as an incredibly brutal massacre committed with assault rifles. The firearms themselves were indeed used quite a bit, by Cleaners attempting desperately trying to hide something.<br /> <br /> One piece of evidence that has always been cited for calling them a cult is the sheer fanaticism that possesses the Cleaners. They have attempted at times to fight groups or entities far more powerful than them in a desperate attempt to hide something. Another incident, this time in the year 1987, involved the Cleaners attempting to slaughter multiple condos worth of Vampires. They failed, owing to that they tried taking on rather powerful Vampires with limited numbers, however in the process, they did cause immense damage to the building, and the event itself that provoked the incident has been lost to time.<br /> <br /> Regardless of their specific motivation, the irony about the Cleaners is, in attempting to hide supernatural events, they have brought a lot of attention to themselves. The mere mention of the Cleaners being in an area can cause multiple Hunter groups, Vampires, Werewolves, Witches, and sometimes far stranger things to appear, looking for them. Some have suggested they do this on purpose to attempt to draw attention away from things, and if so, it may actually work. Its rare for anyone to know why the Cleaners even showed up, if they're aware they are present, and the Cleaners have been known to lead people to dead ends.<br /> <br /> As for where and when the Cleaners have shown up, this has been reduced to speculation. The only known incidents are ones involving mass violence, and even in those, one has to know what to look for. An incident many agree was specifically the fault of the Cleaners, and one that shows their typical handiwork, occurred on a cold night in 2003. Somehow, film has leaked of it, probably recorded by Network Zero, and can be found on Youtube, although it frequently gets taken down.<br /> <br /> It starts, and shows for about two minutes a typical office building. Then, one of the workers transforms into a Werewolf without any real warning. Over the following ten minutes, the creature goes onto massacre most of the floor in some sort of rage. But then, the creature is shot by someone off camera. Entering into frame is someone dressed in the clothing of a typical janitor, wielding some sort of semi-automatic rifle many have theorized to be an M14. The gun is then carefully placed down on a desk, and the Cleaner gets out a variety of equipment to get the place into tidy shape. Most of it is typical cleaning equipment, such as a mop, however, he also gets out a box that somehow becomes a gigantic medical furnace, suitable for destroying biohazard materials.<br /> <br /> The man proceeds to dump all the corpses into the furnace, and any loose guts. The rest is cleaned up using traditional tools, as the werewolf became a normal corpse, easily burned away. Notably, he also destroys any personal artifacts he can find, such as wallets, and destroys all of the clothing in the area. After he finishes, he gets out a phone, and after making a call, leaves the area, taking all the stuff away. Shortly afterwards in the video, another crew of persons arrive. They replace various bits of office equipment with brand new computers, and replace the logo of the corporation with another. They also paint the walls red and white for some reason. The video ends shortly afterwards.<br /> <br /> That office, whomever once owned it, is now owned by a company theorized to be a subsidiary of the Cleaners. This suggests that the Cleaners, if necessary, can acquire private property with ease, and that their income may arise out of a dizzying number of properties they may have acquired from their work. Regardless, the video, which comes in at about 2 hours, shows the full power of the Cleaners, as the nobody can even remember without visual aid what the office once looked like. Additionally, nobody in the video has ever been identified, showing the sheer ability of the Cleaners to remove records and even alter memories when necessary to hide something. Such is the power the Cleaners possess in pursuing their goal, whatever it may be...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 04-03-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:32:52-07:00","id":467914,"title":"","content":"And now I cannot help but thinking in this guy:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/0/9241/279043-71799-butcher-joyce.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:11:06-07:00","id":468007,"title":"","content":"What in the world is that from?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, thoughts on this so far? It is interesting how I might be making an interesting... reverse of sorts for Network Zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:36:29-07:00","id":468022,"title":"","content":"He's from The Darkness. Butcher Joyce by name.<br /> <br /> Also... I have to admit that these guys are leaving me feeling cold in terms of <i>playing</i> them. Compacts and Conspiracies are usually written from the point of view of &quot;this is how much a newbie's going to know&quot;, not from the perspective of outsiders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T18:43:00-07:00","id":468062,"title":"","content":"That... is a good point I admit. But, they aren't done yet, so, I may add some elements to make them feel more playable, along with why the perspective is the way it is perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:38:16-07:00","id":468084,"title":"","content":"And here I got myself thinking this was a Hotline Miami group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:49:41-07:00","id":468092,"title":"","content":"Sorry to be an unintentional tease.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T20:19:50-07:00","id":468099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/462922-conspiracy-the-cleaners?p=468084#post468084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here I got myself thinking this was a Hotline Miami group.</div> </div> </div> </div>The group you're looking for is Revlid's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/344770-repost-revild-s-hotel-mascaron\">Hotel Mascaron</a>. I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T14:53:18-07:00","id":468828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/462922-conspiracy-the-cleaners?p=464092#post464092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting premise. I guess the obvious question is... Why? What do these people gain by this? What ideology motivates someone to kill over this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Money is my first thought but then I started thinking about it more deeply.<br /> <br /> In WoD, The more obvious that the supernatural is, the more likely that things start to hit the crapper. More people get curious, people get hurt or even get killed. Less people who know about it, the less inclined that people are to go fighting it willy nilly and less suffering to be had.<br /> <br /> The Cleaners are basically a human group coming to this train of thought that people can't fuck with what they don't know. Think NIMBYism taken to the extreme. If everyone knows that a murderer is loose in the town, housing prices drop, vigilantes get in the way of law enforcement, lots of bad things hit the average Joe who care less about the metaphysical implications of the world around him and more about why is his bills starting to rise.<br /> <br /> That is not to say that they are MiB or anything of that nature or leave anything intentionally dangerous. For example. A camp ground is dangerous due to a pack of werewolves. Cleaners come, clean up the pack's mess, and putting up signs saying &quot;Beware! Wild Bears!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:07:14-07:00","id":685310,"title":"","content":"Does anybody else can't help but compare these guys to the Cleaners from the Underworld films? Maybe even be inspired by them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:09:00-07:00","id":685316,"title":"","content":"I am suddenly reminded of the Cleaners from Underworld 2 here, which isn't a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T23:30:46-07:00","id":685325,"title":"","content":"I feel like these guys are kinda redundant. I get what they are, but you could easily roll them into any other conspiracy as a separate internal organization with the appropriate lore adjustments. Just off the top of my head, as they are now they sound like either a mercenary compact utilized by TFV to clean up their messes, or as Project: PRICE, dedicated to ensuring the masses can go about their lives without fear of the unknown hanging over their heads. Adjusted for Cheiron, they're probably a little more fast and loose with the cleanup to keep the bottom line acceptable to the vice presidents while still trying to preserve something valuable for study. For the Malleus, you can easily turn them into the thousands of Catholic workers who can be counted on to clean up whatever a priest asks of them.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the concept isn't interesting since someone has to cover this stuff up, but I feel that as a conspiracy on their own they lack a firmer foundation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T18:06:13-07:00","id":700335,"title":"","content":"Good points. <br /> <br /> Originally, this idea sprang up from that I felt like there needed to be more hiding the supernatural from mortals than what the NWOD baseline game provided, hence, a Conspiracy devoted to nothing but hiding stuff. However, that this can somewhat easily be rolled into other conspiracies, or even Compacts depending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}